ary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in v4.5.beta5\nNot Reproducible in v4.4.1.stable, v4.4.0.stable\n\n### System information\n\nFedora Linux 42 (KDE Plasma Desktop Edition)\n\n### Issue description\n\nmain.gd\n```GDScript\nextends Node\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\t_call_threaded()\n\n\nfunc _call_threaded() -> void:\n\tvar object_called_from_thread: RefCounted = load(\"res://object_called_from_thread.gd\").new()\n\tvar task: int = WorkerThreadPool.add_task(object_called_from_thread.task)\n\tawait object_called_from_thread.completed_task\n\tWorkerThreadPool.wait_for_task_completion(task)\n```\nobject_called_from_thread.gd\n```GDScript\nextends RefCounted\n\nsignal completed_task\n\n\nfunc task() -> void:\n\t# [...]\n\tcompleted_task.emit.call_deferred()\n\n```\nError\n> [!CAUTION]\n>  ~Object: Object '<Object#-9223372010464213624>' was freed or unreferenced while a signal is being emitted from it. Try connecting to the signal using 'CONNECT_DEFERRED' flag, or use queue_free() to free the object (if this object is a Node) to avoid this error and potential crashes.\n  <C++ Source>  core/object/object.cpp:2272 @ ~Object()\n\nEmitting the signal normally doesn't cause any errors. Using `await get_tree().process_frame` after receiving the signal and before collecting the thread is also a workaround.\nSince this works fine in 4.4.1 and earlier, I'm unsure if this is a regression or I'm doing something wrong.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nRun the MRP.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[threadedoopsie.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21700205/threadedoopsie.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/follo